{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'rg -n -C 8 \"E15:|re-learning the testing head|Data\" SPEC.md'","aggregated_output":"rg : The term 'rg' is not recognized as the name of a cmdlet, function, script file, or operable program. Check the \r\nspelling of the name, or if a path was included, verify that the path is correct and try again.\r\nAt line:2 char:1\r\n+ rg -n -C 8 \"E15:|re-learning the testing head|Data\" SPEC.md\r\n+ ~~\r\n    + CategoryInfo          : ObjectNotFound: (rg:String) [], CommandNotFoundException\r\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : CommandNotFoundException\r\n \r\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content SPEC.md | Select-String -Pattern 'E15:|re-learning the testing head' -Context 0,40; Get-Content e7_sites.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content SPEC.md | Select-String -Pattern 'E15:|re-learning the testing head' -Context 0,40; Get-Content e7_sites.py\"","aggregated_output":"\r\n> ## E12: re-learning the testing head at B without outcomes (Claude and Wesley, 23 Oct 2026; exploratory, quick \r\nversion)\r\n  \r\n  Question (from a teammate, 22 Oct): rung 3 re-learns only the testing head. The testing head is a likelihood of test \r\norders given the latent state, so it can be fitted on B's records without outcome labels, which exist for every \r\npatient. How does that compare with the labelled rungs, as a function of how much data each uses?\r\n  \r\n  Model: the E5 filter already trained at A (`results/E5/sigma1_gamma2/seed0/filter/params.npz`, sigma 1, A = \r\ninformative gamma 2, rate 0.3). No retraining at A.\r\n  \r\n  Target policies at B (sigma 1, rate 0.3 unless stated): `B_less` informative gamma 1 (less selective); `B_more` \r\ninformative gamma 3.5 (more selective; the dial in [0, 1] cannot help here, see docs/GAP.md \"The dial above 1\"); \r\n`B_match` uniform 0.3; `B_dense` uniform 0.6.\r\n  \r\n  Data at B: test cohort n = 8,000 (E5 test latent seed, new observation seed per policy); labelled run-in pools and \r\nunlabelled pools from new latent seeds, disjoint from the test cohort. Outcome prevalence is about 16%.\r\n  \r\n  Methods (all start from the A parameters; only the testing-head logits c, 32 numbers, or w change):\r\n  - `keep`: w = 1. `drop`: w = 0.\r\n  - `dial_L` (rung 1): w on the grid 0, 0.05, ..., 1 minimising log loss on the labelled run-in (ties to 1).\r\n  - `head_L` (rung 3, labelled): refit c on the labelled run-in with the E5 training loss (BCE + per-step NLL of \r\nvalues and masks), all other parameters frozen.\r\n  - `head_U` (rung 3, no outcomes): refit c on an unlabelled pool by the per-step NLL of values and masks only, all \r\nother parameters frozen.\r\n  - `oracle`: exact Bayes predictor under the B policy (`bayes.bayes_predict`).\r\n  Refits: Adam lr 1e-2, minibatch 256, 80 steps, initialised at A's c; no early stopping.\r\n  \r\n  Sizes: labelled run-in n_L = 30, 125, 500 patients (about 5, 20, 80 outcome cases); unlabelled pool n_U = 200, 2,000 \r\npatients. 3 draws per size and policy. Quick version; more draws only if the answer is unclear.\r\n  \r\n  Outputs: per policy, method, size and draw: Brier, log loss, AUROC on the B test cohort, and regret = Brier minus \r\noracle Brier; the refitted c curves for `head_U` at n_U = 2,000 against the true B testing curve on the latent grid \r\n(sanity check; states need not align, see E5). Files `analysis/e12_runs.csv`, `analysis/e12_summary.csv`, \r\n`analysis/e12_c_curves.csv`.\r\n  \r\n  Expectation, stated in advance: in this simulator testing depends only on the latent state, so B's change of policy \r\nis the case `head_U` is built for; it should approach the oracle without labels, and handle `B_more`, where the dial \r\ncannot. A shift in what a test means for the outcome beyond the state cannot be simulated here, and `head_U` would not \r\ndetect it.\r\n  \r\n  ## E13: which rung when? Performance over weeks of deployment (Claude and Wesley, 23 Oct 2026; simulation)\r\n  \r\n  Question: as data from hospital B accrue week by week after deployment, which rung of the ladder is best at each \r\ntime, and where do the curves cross? Main figure: x = weeks since deployment (log scale), y = regret against the exact \r\noptimum at B, one curve per rung, the best rung per week shaded.\r\n  \r\n  Ladder (ordered by outcome labels needed; Wesley, 23 Oct; docs/ARGUMENT.md section 10):\r\n  - R0 `keep`: A's model.\r\n  - R1 `head_U`: re-learn the testing-head logits c on all of B's records so far, without outcomes (value-and-mask \r\nlikelihood only), other parameters frozen.\r\n  - R2 `head_U_dial`: R1, then one weight w in [0, 1] on the re-learned testing evidence, chosen on the labelled \r\npatients so far by penalised log loss: sum of log losses + 2 * (w - 1)^2 (E9's prior, sd 0.5 around 1); no outcome \r\ncase yet -> w = 1.\r\n  - R4 `finetune`: all parameters from A's values, on the labelled patients so far, loss BCE + per-step NLL (E5 loss); \r\nno outcome case yet -> A's model.\r\n  - Baseline `dial_only`: the original dial on A's model (no re-learning), same penalised rule as R2.\r\n  - R3 (dial per test group) needs several tests; the simulator has one. Left for the multi-test simulator.\r\n  - `oracle`: exact Bayes predictor under B's policy.\r\n  \r\n  Realistic rates: outcome threshold raised from 1.0 to 2.05 so that about 2% of patients have the outcome (as sepsis \r\nin E6). This changes the A model: retrain the E5 filter at A (informative gamma 2, rate 0.3, sigma 1) with this \r\noutcome, n_train 16,000, n_val 4,000 (about 320 and 80 cases), otherwise as E5 (`latent_filter.train_filter`). \r\nImplementation: set `sim.THRESHOLD` and `bayes.THRESHOLD` (bayes imports it by value) to 2.05 at import time of the \r\nE13 script, so spawned workers see it too.\r\n  \r\n  Time axis: weeks t = 1, 2, 4, 8, 13, 26, 52, 104; 25 admissions per week (1,300 a year, a median US ICU), so n(t) = \r\n25 t patients (about 0.5 outcome cases a week). All n(t) patients' testing records are available for R1; their \r\noutcomes are available for R2, R4 and `dial_only` (outcome delay ignored: the 6-hour horizon is short against a week).\r\n  \r\n> ## E15: re-learning the testing head on real hospital pairs (Claude and Wesley, 25 Oct 2026; exploratory pilot, \r\nquick version)\r\n  \r\n  Question: does head_U (re-learn the testing part from the target's records without outcomes) help on real pairs \r\nwhere E10 found the testing pattern's meaning shifted, and does it do no harm where it did not? This is the first run \r\nof the state-space model on real data.\r\n  \r\n  Model (`latent_filter_mv.py`, new; `latent_filter.py` unchanged): the E5 filter for D variables. K = 32 discrete \r\nstates, learned transition and initial distribution (initialised as E5), per variable d a Gaussian value head (mean \r\nmu[k, d], log sd per variable), a testing head c[k, d] (P(variable d measured in hour t | state k) = sigmoid(c[k, \r\nd])), outcome head u[k] read from the final filtered belief. Values and tests of different variables are independent \r\ngiven the state. The weight w multiplies the summed testing log-likelihood (w in [0, 1]). Loss: BCE + lambda * \r\n(negative log marginal) / (T * D), lambda = 1 by default (flag). Sanity requirement: on the source's validation split \r\nthe model's AUROC should be within about 0.05 of E7's linear model with pattern features (from `analysis/e7_*`); \r\nreport both. If it is far below, stop and report rather than continue.\r\n  \r\n  Data (`e15_sequences.py`, new): hourly sequences for the E7 cohorts (same inclusion rules and patient ids, read \r\n`e7_sites.py`). PhysioNet 2019: hours 1-24, outcome sepsis in hours 25-72, sites `A-all` and `B-all` (whole hospitals, \r\nA = Beth Israel, B = Emory, union of E7's unit cohorts). PhysioNet 2012: hours 0-47 binned hourly (last value in the \r\nhour; measured = any value in the hour), outcome in-hospital death, sites CCU, CSRU, MICU, SICU. Variables: all \r\ntime-varying vitals and labs of the dataset (no static variables). Values: impossible values set to missing (pH \r\noutside 6.5-8.0 and any negative value of a nonnegative variable); log1p for variables positive and right-skewed in \r\nthe pooled data (skewness above 2, list recorded in the cache); standardisation with the source's training split (done \r\nin the experiment, not the cache); standardised values clipped to [-5, 5]. Cache `data/e15_cache.npz`: per site x [n, \r\nT, D] float32 with NaN, m [n, T, D] int8, y, patient ids, variable names, log list.\r\n  \r\n  Pairs (from E10's pattern gaps): shift pairs P12 SICU to CSRU, CSRU to CCU, CSRU to SICU, CCU to SICU, P19 B-all to \r\nA-all; control pairs (no pattern shift) P12 MICU to SICU, SICU to MICU, P19 A-all to B-all (the E6 pair). Sources: 6 A \r\nmodels (P12 CCU, CSRU, MICU, SICU; P19 A-all, B-all), each trained once on an 80/20 train/validation split (fixed \r\nseed), cached under `results/E15/a_model_<dataset>_<site>/`.\r\n  \r\n  Target split: fixed 50/50 into a pool and an evaluation half (fixed seed). Run-ins drawn without replacement from \r\nthe pool: n_run = 162 and 650 (3 and 12 months of a typical ICU, as E8/E11), 3 draws each (quick).\r\n  \r\n  Methods (same definitions as E14 where they exist; refits 160 steps, minibatch 256 with replacement, lr 0.05 for \r\nhead refits, lr 0.005 for fine-tuning):\r\n  - `keep` (w = 1), `drop` (w = 0, Futoma), `dial_only` (penalised w in [0, 1] on the run-in, E13 rule);\r\n  - `head_U` (testing heads c re-learned on the run-in records, no outcomes), `head_U_pool` (the same on the whole \r\npool without outcomes: B's historical records, available before deployment);\r\n  - `head_L` (c re-learned on the run-in with outcomes, BCE + NLL), `finetune` (all parameters on the run-in, lr \r\n0.005).\r\n  Primary metric AUROC on the evaluation half (difference to `keep`), secondary log loss. Exploratory: no \r\npre-specified primary test; the quick version is a pilot to decide whether to run 20 draws and more pairs.\r\n  \r\n  Expectation, stated in advance: on the shift pairs head_U and head_U_pool beat keep where the shift is in how \r\ntesting depends on the patient's measured state; on the control pairs they stay within about 0.005 of keep. If the \r\nshift pairs show no gain, the E10 shift is of the kind only outcomes reveal (E14's `gain`).\r\n\"\"\"Build E7 PhysioNet site cohorts with raw (unimputed, unscaled) features.\"\"\"\r\n\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nimport json\r\nimport time\r\nimport warnings\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nimport numpy as np\r\nimport pandas as pd\r\n\r\n\r\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\r\nP19_RAW = ROOT / \"data\" / \"raw_physionet2019\"\r\nP12_RAW = ROOT / \"data\" / \"raw_physionet2012\"\r\nCACHE = ROOT / \"data\" / \"e7_cache.npz\"\r\n\r\nP19_VITAL_LABS = [\r\n    \"HR\", \"O2Sat\", \"Temp\", \"SBP\", \"MAP\", \"DBP\", \"Resp\", \"EtCO2\",\r\n    \"BaseExcess\", \"HCO3\", \"FiO2\", \"pH\", \"PaCO2\", \"SaO2\", \"AST\", \"BUN\",\r\n    \"Alkalinephos\", \"Calcium\", \"Chloride\", \"Creatinine\", \"Bilirubin_direct\",\r\n    \"Glucose\", \"Lactate\", \"Magnesium\", \"Phosphate\", \"Potassium\",\r\n    \"Bilirubin_total\", \"TroponinI\", \"Hct\", \"Hgb\", \"PTT\", \"WBC\",\r\n    \"Fibrinogen\", \"Platelets\",\r\n]\r\nP19_DEMOGRAPHICS = [\"Age\", \"Gender\", \"HospAdmTime\"]\r\nP19_COLUMNS = P19_VITAL_LABS + P19_DEMOGRAPHICS + [\"ICULOS\", \"SepsisLabel\", \"Unit1\", \"Unit2\"]\r\nP12_STATIC = [\"RecordID\", \"Age\", \"Gender\", \"Height\", \"ICUType\", \"Weight\"]\r\nP12_SITE_NAMES = {1: \"CCU\", 2: \"CSRU\", 3: \"MICU\", 4: \"SICU\"}\r\nP19_SITE_NAMES = [(\"A-MICU\", \"A\", \"MICU\"), (\"A-SICU\", \"A\", \"SICU\"),\r\n                  (\"B-MICU\", \"B\", \"MICU\"), (\"B-SICU\", \"B\", \"SICU\")]\r\nCACHE_VERSION = 1\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _last_finite(values: np.ndarray, rows: np.ndarray) -> float:\r\n    v = values[rows]\r\n    good = np.flatnonzero(np.isfinite(v))\r\n    return float(v[good[-1]]) if len(good) else np.nan\r\n\r\n\r\ndef build_p19() -> dict:\r\n    started = time.perf_counter()\r\n    if not (P19_RAW / \"training_setA\").is_dir() or not (P19_RAW / \"training_setB\").is_dir():\r\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Expected P19 training_setA and training_setB below {P19_RAW}\")\r\n    groups = {name: {\"phys\": [], \"pattern\": [], \"y\": [], \"ids\": []} for name, _, _ in P19_SITE_NAMES}\r\n    exclusions = {\"missing_hours_1_24\": 0, \"early_sepsis\": 0, \"neither_unit\": 0,\r\n                  \"ambiguous_both_units\": 0}\r\n    file_counts = {\"A\": 0, \"B\": 0}\r\n    for hospital, folder_name in ((\"A\", \"training_setA\"), (\"B\", \"training_setB\")):\r\n        paths = sorted((P19_RAW / folder_name).glob(\"*.psv\"))\r\n        file_counts[hospital] = len(paths)\r\n        for i, path in enumerate(paths, 1):\r\n            df = pd.read_csv(path, sep=\"|\", usecols=P19_COLUMNS, dtype=np.float32, na_values=[\"NaN\"])\r\n            icu = df[\"ICULOS\"].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32, copy=False)\r\n            labels = df[\"SepsisLabel\"].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32, copy=False)\r\n            feature_rows = np.isfinite(icu) & (icu >= 1) & (icu <= 24)\r\n            hours = icu[feature_rows].astype(np.int16)\r\n            if not np.all(np.isin(np.arange(1, 25), hours)):\r\n                exclusions[\"missing_hours_1_24\"] += 1\r\n                continue\r\n            if np.any(labels[feature_rows] == 1):\r\n                exclusions[\"early_sepsis\"] += 1\r\n                continue\r\n\r\n            # Unit indicators are static in practice; use the first row in the\r\n            # feature window where at least one indicator is recorded.\r\n            u1 = df[\"Unit1\"].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32, copy=False)\r\n            u2 = df[\"Unit2\"].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32, copy=False)\r\n            unit_rows = np.flatnonzero(feature_rows & (np.isfinite(u1) | np.isfinite(u2)))\r\n            if not len(unit_rows):\r\n                exclusions[\"neither_unit\"] += 1\r\n                continue\r\n            row = int(unit_rows[0])\r\n            one = np.isfinite(u1[row]) and u1[row] == 1\r\n            two = np.isfinite(u2[row]) and u2[row] == 1\r\n            if not one and not two:\r\n                exclusions[\"neither_unit\"] += 1\r\n                continue\r\n            if one and two:\r\n                exclusions[\"ambiguous_both_units\"] += 1\r\n            unit = \"MICU\" if one else \"SICU\"\r\n            site = f\"{hospital}-{unit}\"\r\n\r\n            physiology = np.full(len(P19_VITAL_LABS) + len(P19_DEMOGRAPHICS), np.nan, dtype=np.float64)\r\n            observed = np.zeros((int(feature_rows.sum()), len(P19_VITAL_LABS)), dtype=bool)\r\n            for j, col in enumerate(P19_VITAL_LABS):\r\n                vals = df[col].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32, copy=False)\r\n                physiology[j] = _last_finite(vals, feature_rows)\r\n                observed[:, j] = np.isfinite(vals[feature_rows])\r\n            for j, col in enumerate(P19_DEMOGRAPHICS):\r\n                vals = df[col].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32, copy=False)\r\n                physiology[len(P19_VITAL_LABS) + j] = _last_finite(vals, feature_rows)\r\n            recent_rows = icu[feature_rows] >= 17\r\n            pattern = np.concatenate((\r\n                observed[recent_rows].any(axis=0).astype(np.float64),\r\n                observed.any(axis=0).astype(np.float64),\r\n                [np.log1p(int(observed.sum()))],\r\n            ))\r\n            outcome_rows = np.isfinite(icu) & (icu >= 25) & (icu <= 72)\r\n            y = int(np.any(labels[outcome_rows] == 1))\r\n            groups[site][\"phys\"].append(physiology)\r\n            groups[site][\"pattern\"].append(pattern)\r\n            groups[site][\"y\"].append(y)\r\n            groups[site][\"ids\"].append(f\"{hospital}:{path.stem}\")\r\n            if i % 5000 == 0:\r\n                print(f\"P19 {hospital}: read {i:,}/{len(paths):,} files\", flush=True)\r\n\r\n    out = {}\r\n    for name, values in groups.items():\r\n        out[name] = {\r\n            \"raw_phys\": np.asarray(values[\"phys\"], dtype=np.float64).reshape((-1, len(P19_VITAL_LABS) + len(P19_DEMOGRAPHICS))),\r\n            \"raw_pattern\": np.asarray(values[\"pattern\"], dtype=np.float64).reshape((-1, 2 * len(P19_VITAL_LABS) + 1)),\r\n            \"y\": np.asarray(values[\"y\"], dtype=np.uint8),\r\n            \"patient_ids\": np.asarray(values[\"ids\"], dtype=\"U40\"),\r\n        }\r\n    info = {\r\n        \"file_counts\": file_counts,\r\n        \"exclusions\": exclusions,\r\n        \"feature_window_iculos\": [1, 24],\r\n        \"outcome_window_iculos\": [25, 72],\r\n        \"features_use_iculos_1_24_only\": True,\r\n        \"phys_names\": P19_VITAL_LABS + [f\"{v}^2\" for v in P19_VITAL_LABS] + P19_DEMOGRAPHICS,\r\n        \"raw_phys_names\": P19_VITAL_LABS + P19_DEMOGRAPHICS,\r\n        \"pattern_names\": ([f\"recent_{v}\" for v in P19_VITAL_LABS]\r\n                           + [f\"ever_{v}\" for v in P19_VITAL_LABS]\r\n                           + [\"log1p_total_measurements_1_24\"]),\r\n        \"build_seconds\": time.perf_counter() - started,\r\n    }\r\n    return out, info\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _parse_time(value: str) -> float:\r\n    parts = str(value).split(\":\")\r\n    if len(parts) != 2:\r\n        return np.nan\r\n    try:\r\n        return float(parts[0]) + float(parts[1]) / 60.0\r\n    except ValueError:\r\n        return np.nan\r\n\r\n\r\ndef build_p12() -> dict:\r\n    started = time.perf_counter()\r\n    if not P12_RAW.is_dir():\r\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Expected P12 directory {P12_RAW}\")\r\n    records = []\r\n    dynamic_vars = set()\r\n    problems = {\"missing_outcome\": 0, \"missing_icu_type\": 0, \"invalid_icu_type\": 0,\r\n                \"missing_static_age\": 0, \"missing_static_gender\": 0,\r\n                \"missing_static_height\": 0, \"missing_static_weight\": 0}\r\n    for set_letter in (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"):\r\n        folder = P12_RAW / f\"set-{set_letter}\"\r\n        outcome_path = P12_RAW / f\"Outcomes-{set_letter}.txt\"\r\n        if not folder.is_dir() or not outcome_path.is_file():\r\n            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Missing P12 input for set {set_letter}\")\r\n        outcome_df = pd.read_csv(outcome_path)\r\n        outcome_map = dict(zip(outcome_df[\"RecordID\"].astype(int), outcome_df[\"In-hospital_death\"].astype(int)))\r\n        paths = sorted(folder.glob(\"*.txt\"))\r\n        for i, path in enumerate(paths, 1):\r\n            record_id = int(path.stem)\r\n            if record_id not in outcome_map:\r\n                problems[\"missing_outcome\"] += 1\r\n                continue\r\n            df = pd.read_csv(path, dtype={\"Time\": str, \"Parameter\": str})\r\n            df[\"hour\"] = df[\"Time\"].map(_parse_time)\r\n            # The feature dictionary is the cohort-wide set of time-varying\r\n            # variables; values and measurement patterns are still windowed.\r\n            dynamic_vars.update(\r\n                df.loc[~df[\"Parameter\"].isin(P12_STATIC), \"Parameter\"].dropna().astype(str).tolist()\r\n            )\r\n            static = {}\r\n            for key in (\"Age\", \"Gender\", \"Height\", \"ICUType\", \"Weight\"):\r\n                vals = pd.to_numeric(df.loc[(df[\"Time\"] == \"00:00\") & (df[\"Parameter\"] == key), \"Value\"], errors=\"coerce\")\r\n                val = float(vals.iloc[0]) if len(vals) else np.nan\r\n                if key != \"ICUType\" and val == -1:\r\n                    val = np.nan\r\n                static[key] = val\r\n            icu_value = static[\"ICUType\"]\r\n            if not np.isfinite(icu_value):\r\n                problems[\"missing_icu_type\"] += 1\r\n                continue\r\n            site_type = int(icu_value)\r\n            if site_type not in P12_SITE_NAMES:\r\n                problems[\"invalid_icu_type\"] += 1\r\n                continue\r\n            for key in (\"Age\", \"Gender\", \"Height\", \"Weight\"):\r\n                if not np.isfinite(static[key]):\r\n                    problems[f\"missing_static_{key.lower()}\"] += 1\r\n            within = np.isfinite(df[\"hour\"].to_numpy(dtype=np.float64)) & (df[\"hour\"].to_numpy(dtype=np.float64) >= 0) & (df[\"hour\"].to_numpy(dtype=np.float64) <= 48)\r\n            dyn_df = df.loc[within & ~df[\"Parameter\"].isin(P12_STATIC)]\r\n            by_var: dict[str, tuple[float, bool, bool, float]] = {}\r\n            for parameter, part in dyn_df.groupby(\"Parameter\", sort=False):\r\n                name = str(parameter)\r\n                if name in P12_STATIC:\r\n                    continue\r\n                hours = part[\"hour\"].to_numpy(dtype=np.float64)\r\n                values = pd.to_numeric(part[\"Value\"], errors=\"coerce\").to_numpy(dtype=np.float64)\r\n                finite = np.isfinite(values)\r\n                valid = np.flatnonzero(finite)\r\n                if len(valid):\r\n                    latest_hour = np.max(hours[valid])\r\n                    latest_rows = valid[hours[valid] == latest_hour]\r\n                    last = float(values[latest_rows[-1]])\r\n                else:\r\n                    last = np.nan\r\n                ever = len(part) > 0\r\n                recent = bool(np.any((hours >= 40.0) & (hours <= 48.0)))\r\n                count = float(len(part))\r\n                by_var[name] = (last, recent, ever, count)\r\n            records.append({\r\n                \"set\": set_letter,\r\n                \"record_id\": record_id,\r\n                \"patient_id\": f\"{set_letter}:{record_id}\",\r\n                \"site\": P12_SITE_NAMES[site_type],\r\n                \"static\": static,\r\n                \"dynamic\": by_var,\r\n                \"y\": int(outcome_map[record_id]),\r\n            })\r\n            if i % 1000 == 0:\r\n                print(f\"P12 set-{set_letter}: read {i:,}/{len(paths):,} stays\", flush=True)\r\n\r\n    variables = sorted(dynamic_vars)\r\n    sites = sorted(P12_SITE_NAMES.values())\r\n    output = {}\r\n    phys_names = variables + [f\"{v}^2\" for v in variables] + [\"Age\", \"Gender\", \"Height\", \"Weight\"]\r\n    pattern_names = ([f\"recent_{v}\" for v in variables] + [f\"ever_{v}\" for v in variables]\r\n                     + [\"log1p_total_measurements_0_48\"])\r\n    for site in sites:\r\n        selected = [r for r in records if r[\"site\"] == site]\r\n        n, nv = len(selected), len(variables)\r\n        raw_phys = np.full((n, nv + 4), np.nan, dtype=np.float64)\r\n        raw_pattern = np.zeros((n, 2 * nv + 1), dtype=np.float64)\r\n        y = np.empty(n, dtype=np.uint8)\r\n        patient_ids = []\r\n        for i, record in enumerate(selected):\r\n            counts = 0.0\r\n            for j, name in enumerate(variables):\r\n                last, recent, ever, count = record[\"dynamic\"].get(name, (np.nan, False, False, 0.0))\r\n                raw_phys[i, j] = last\r\n                raw_pattern[i, j] = float(recent)\r\n                raw_pattern[i, nv + j] = float(ever)\r\n                counts += count\r\n            raw_pattern[i, -1] = np.log1p(counts)\r\n            for j, key in enumerate((\"Age\", \"Gender\", \"Height\", \"Weight\")):\r\n                raw_phys[i, nv + j] = record[\"static\"][key]\r\n            y[i] = record[\"y\"]\r\n            patient_ids.append(record[\"patient_id\"])\r\n        output[site] = {\"raw_phys\": raw_phys, \"raw_pattern\": raw_pattern, \"y\": y,\r\n                        \"patient_ids\": np.asarray(patient_ids, dtype=\"U24\")}\r\n    info = {\r\n        \"file_counts\": {letter: sum(1 for _ in (P12_RAW / f\"set-{letter}\").glob(\"*.txt\")) for letter in \"abc\"},\r\n        \"included_records\": len(records),\r\n        \"exclusions_and_missing_static\": problems,\r\n        \"feature_window_hours\": [0, 48],\r\n        \"recent_pattern_window_hours\": [40, 48],\r\n        \"features_use_hours_0_48_only\": True,\r\n        \"phys_names\": phys_names,\r\n        \"raw_phys_names\": variables + [\"Age\", \"Gender\", \"Height\", \"Weight\"],\r\n        \"pattern_names\": pattern_names,\r\n        \"time_varying_variables\": variables,\r\n        \"weight_static_at_00_00_only\": True,\r\n        \"build_seconds\": time.perf_counter() - started,\r\n    }\r\n    return output, info\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _pack_dataset(arrays: dict, names: list[str], dataset: str, payload: dict) -> None:\r\n    for site, values in arrays.items():\r\n        prefix = f\"{dataset}_{site}\"\r\n        payload[f\"{prefix}_raw_phys\"] = values[\"raw_phys\"].astype(np.float32)\r\n        payload[f\"{prefix}_raw_pattern\"] = values[\"raw_pattern\"].astype(np.float32)\r\n        payload[f\"{prefix}_y\"] = values[\"y\"].astype(np.uint8)\r\n        payload[f\"{prefix}_patient_ids\"] = values[\"patient_ids\"]\r\n    payload[f\"{dataset}_sites\"] = np.asarray(list(arrays), dtype=\"U16\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main() -> None:\r\n    started = time.perf_counter()\r\n    p19, p19_info = build_p19()\r\n    p12, p12_info = build_p12()\r\n    payload = {}\r\n    _pack_dataset(p19, list(p19), \"P19\", payload)\r\n    _pack_dataset(p12, list(p12), \"P12\", payload)\r\n    metadata = {\"cache_version\": CACHE_VERSION, \"P19\": p19_info, \"P12\": p12_info,\r\n                \"cache_built_utc\": time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\", time.gmtime()),\r\n                \"total_build_seconds\": time.perf_counter() - started}\r\n    payload[\"P19_phys_names\"] = np.asarray(p19_info[\"phys_names\"], dtype=\"U64\")\r\n    payload[\"P19_raw_phys_names\"] = np.asarray(p19_info[\"raw_phys_names\"], dtype=\"U64\")\r\n    payload[\"P19_pattern_names\"] = np.asarray(p19_info[\"pattern_names\"], dtype=\"U64\")\r\n    payload[\"P12_phys_names\"] = np.asarray(p12_info[\"phys_names\"], dtype=\"U64\")\r\n    payload[\"P12_raw_phys_names\"] = np.asarray(p12_info[\"raw_phys_names\"], dtype=\"U96\")\r\n    payload[\"P12_pattern_names\"] = np.asarray(p12_info[\"pattern_names\"], dtype=\"U96\")\r\n    payload[\"meta_json\"] = np.asarray(json.dumps(metadata, separators=(\",\", \":\")), dtype=\"U\")\r\n    CACHE.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\r\n    np.savez_compressed(CACHE, **payload)\r\n    print(\"E7 cohorts (n, outcome cases)\", flush=True)\r\n    for ds, arrays in ((\"P19\", p19), (\"P12\", p12)):\r\n        for site, values in arrays.items():\r\n            print(f\"{ds} {site}: n={len(values['y']):,}, cases={int(values['y'].sum()):,}\", flush=True)\r\n    print(f\"P19 exclusions: {p19_info['exclusions']}\", flush=True)\r\n    print(f\"P12 data checks: {p12_info['exclusions_and_missing_static']}\", flush=True)\r\n    print(f\"P12 time-varying variables={len(p12_info['time_varying_variables'])}\", flush=True)\r\n    print(f\"Cached raw feature matrices: {CACHE} ({CACHE.stat().st_size / 1024**2:.1f} MiB)\", flush=True)\r\n    print(f\"E7 cohort build runtime: {metadata['total_build_seconds'] / 60:.1f} min\", flush=True)\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    main()\r\n\r\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
